Author: Makapania <matt.sponheimer@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat May 2 13:33:46 2026 -0600

    fix(T-19): library-aware class_weight injection in exported code
    
    Pre-T-19 the catch-all branch in code_generator._render_model() unconditionally
    injected class_weight='balanced' into every classifier's __init__ params:
    
    - LightGBM, RandomForest, sklearn LR/SVC: works (native kwarg)
    - XGBoost: silently ignored at fit time (no balancing actually applied)
    - CatBoost: hard TypeError on instantiation
    
    Dispatch per library:
    - CatBoost gets auto_class_weights='Balanced'
    - XGBoost gets sample_weight=compute_sample_weight('balanced', y) threaded
      into the CV-fold and final-model fit() calls (mirrors runtime path)
    - Other libraries keep class_weight='balanced'
    
    Pipeline behavior unchanged for users not using imbalance_method='class_weight'.
    For users who do, exported scripts now actually run (CatBoost) and actually
    weight the loss (XGBoost) — matching runtime dasp behavior. Pinned with
    13 regression tests including end-to-end exec of the generated scripts.

